t unblocking the cascade requires the epic to earn a certified PASS attestation (not merely admission), and note that rewriting the description may surface new blocking findings and/or require a separate sign-review step to persist the attestation.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'runs `rebar review-plan` to earn the attestation that unblocks the cascade' — treats admission and earning an attestation as one step","AC2 only checks 'no P4 admission finding'; AC3 checks 'claim ... exits 0', which requires a certified PASS attestation on the parent","The parent epic 0e68 currently has signature null / no plan-review attestation; the cascade error is 'no certified plan-review attestation'","lamprey's own comment records a PASS whose attestation 'could not persist ... after 3 attempts' and needed a separate `sign-review` step — admission does not imply a persisted PASS"],"finding":"The mechanism from AC2 (review-plan admits the plan) to AC3 (claim exits 0) is incomplete: clearing the P4 admission cap only lets the review RUN; it does not guarantee a PASS verdict nor a persisted/signed attestation, both of which the parent-first cascade requires before a child can be claimed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc3883da5b0dfbb69","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + Acceptance Criteria (AC2, AC3)","norm_id":"nc6fd670bd1946bcd","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["After trimming, review-plan admits the plan but returns blocking (non-P4) findings on the rewritten description, so no PASS attestation is produced and AC3 still fails","Review passes but the attestation fails to persist, requiring a separate sign step the plan never mentions"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an intermediate criterion: `rebar review-plan 0e68-41eb-5782-4336` returns a certified PASS with zero blocking findings and a persisted plan-review attestation on the epic, before AC3's claim check.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the exact invalidation scope of editing the epic description on sibling children's attestations, and state how affected siblings are re-attested so the fix does not merely relocate the blockage.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'the material change would invalidate any plan-review attestation already held by its other children'","The plan uses this only to justify who does the work, not to handle the resulting re-blocking of other children","Whether a parent-description edit actually invalidates a child's attestation is a load-bearing codebase fact (child manifests hash the child's own material, e.g. lamprey's 'material-part: description'), and the plan asserts invalidation without reconciling it"],"finding":"The approach acknowledges that editing the epic description 'would invalidate any plan-rev